# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line-ending policy.
#
# THE PROBLEM THIS FIXES: the repository's committed blobs are LF, but the
# Windows working tree had been rewritten to CRLF. Every one of ~72 tracked
# files therefore reported as modified while being semantically identical
# (`git diff --ignore-all-space` was empty). Any `git add -A` would have swept
# them all into whatever commit happened to be in progress.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes to LF in the object database and checks out LF,
# which matches what is already committed. Nothing in the repository is
# content-changed by this; the diff noise simply stops.
#
# Binary assets are listed explicitly so nothing tries to normalize a JPEG.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* text=auto eol=lf

*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
